{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109548-dead-metis-storage-questions","id":1109548,"title":"\"Dead Metis Storage\" Questions.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-29T19:23:20-07:00","id":1109548,"title":"\"Dead Metis Storage\" Questions.","content":"(Evil chuckle) After re-visiting an old &quot;Pulp Fiction&quot; inspired post I made a couple of months ago....<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1007357-inspiration-for-werewolf?p=1078780#post1078780\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...80#post1078780</a><br /> <br /> A few questions about &quot;Dead Metis Storage&quot;<br /> <br /> 1A) Can the average dead metis fit inside the trunk of a car?<br /> 1B) And if so, would it be a viable method of disposal to drive said car to a &quot;car compacting facility&quot;, have the car cubed and melted like in &quot;Goldfinger&quot;, right?<br /> <br /> 2A) Would a dead metis corpse (being Crinos) still invoke The Delirium if spotted by a human who catches you dragging it across the road?<br /> 2B) If not, would it be an efficient idea to have said Metis be dried, stuffed, taxidermied and passed off as an exhibit in a wax-museum/theme-restaurant/circus/roller coaster ride? As a prop, it would be the perfect cover, wouldn't it?<br /> <br /> Ah Tarantino Films; inspiring stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 06-29-2017, 11:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T06:31:49-07:00","id":1109725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109548-dead-metis-storage-questions#post1109548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Evil chuckle) After re-visiting an old &quot;Pulp Fiction&quot; inspired post I made a couple of months ago....<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1007357-inspiration-for-werewolf?p=1078780#post1078780\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...80#post1078780</a><br /> <br /> A few questions about &quot;Dead Metis Storage&quot;<br /> <br /> 1A) Can the average dead metis fit inside the trunk of a car?<br /> 1B) And if so, would it be a viable method of disposal to drive said car to a &quot;car compacting facility&quot;, have the car cubed and melted like in &quot;Goldfinger&quot;, right?<br /> <br /> 2A) Would a dead metis corpse (being Crinos) still invoke The Delirium if spotted by a human who catches you dragging it across the road?<br /> 2B) If not, would it be an efficient idea to have said Metis be dried, stuffed, taxidermied and passed off as an exhibit in a wax-museum/theme-restaurant/circus/roller coaster ride? As a prop, it would be the perfect cover, wouldn't it?<br /> <br /> Ah Tarantino Films; inspiring stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>1A.<br /> I think you'd have to dismember it but...maybe? The problem is the weight. You could fill a trunk with clothing but I wouldn't even try to fill one with books. At 900 lbs...that's a lot of weight. You generally need a trailer for that.<br /> <br /> 1B.<br /> Sure. meat is meat.<br /> <br /> 2A.<br /> Imma go with conditional Yes. If it's like a scene from a horror movie, they make a delirium roll, but if you're just driving it down the street in a shopping cart, no.<br /> <br /> 2B.<br /> No because it would still be a Veil breach. Hunters would see it and want to investigate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T12:30:49-07:00","id":1109864,"title":"","content":"I think that you generally want a truck or a van to deal with the dead Metis (moving the body is a bit of a problem unless you have a couple of Crinos). Alternatively, you can dismember the corpse and divide it among multiple cars. Either way, there is going to be a mess. I would suggest that every Sept outside of the Red Talons possesses a group of Human Kinfolk with the right equipment who are trained to take care of the problem should it arise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T13:19:27-07:00","id":1109896,"title":"","content":"There is a rite that will make a dead Metis corpse appear as either human or wolf. Unless you have a heavy duty vehicle you're going to have major issues fitting and carrying a 9ft tall cadaver. If the corpse doesn't instill the Delerium on onlookers having it stuffed would be a profoundly bad idea. Not only a veil breach as previously stated, but making the genetic material readily available for sampling is also bad. Finally, I know Metis get treated like crap by the Garou but even the most obstinate of Fianna isn't going to disrespect a corpse like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T17:32:45-07:00","id":1109976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109548-dead-metis-storage-questions?p=1109864#post1109864\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would suggest that every Sept outside of the Red Talons possesses a group of Human Kinfolk with the right equipment who are trained to take care of the problem should it arise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, a Kinfolk &quot;Cleaner&quot; based on Harvey Keitel's &quot;The Wolf&quot; (Hehehe... the irony) whom stupid young GAROU have to defer to if they don't want a veil-breach on Fox News the next day.... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> For the septs that DO have the right number of Garou available, though; which Auspice would be more suited to the &quot;Cleaner&quot; role? Theurge or Philodox?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T17:42:35-07:00","id":1109978,"title":"","content":"I imagine that the Theurge would get the job because they deal with spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T17:45:19-07:00","id":1109979,"title":"","content":"On a more serious note:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109548-dead-metis-storage-questions?p=1109896#post1109896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...but even the most obstinate of Fianna isn't going to disrespect a corpse like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Those alcoholic Irish whoremongers practically consider Metis little better than Black Spiral Dancers that can be kept on a short leash from <i>birth</i>, beat them and bully them ALL childhood, and make crawl through broken glass for the basic <i>scraps</i> of kindness and respect, and THEN coldly-shrug &quot;they are corrupt anyway&quot; when they dance the spiral as a KINDER alternative to the Fianna life.<br /> <br /> If they don't even respect or show basic-kindness to their designated tribal &quot;trash&quot; in life, even as <i>children</i>, what if any reason is there that they'll respect them in death?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 07-01-2017, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T19:26:28-07:00","id":1110010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109548-dead-metis-storage-questions?p=1109979#post1109979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they don't even respect or show basic-kindness to their designated tribal &quot;trash&quot; in life, even as <i>children</i>, what if any reason is there that they'll respect them in death?</div> </div> </div> </div>In death, a member of Project Mayhem has a name! His name is Robert Paulson!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12777,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","user":"Wakuwa","date":". 06-30-2017, 10:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","name":"Wakuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12777_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T20:16:32-07:00","id":1110028,"title":"","content":"Is it wrong that I chuckled when I read the title of this thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my DriveThruRPG books at: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Carrie%20Kube\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....=Carrie%20Kube</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1834-yaoi-huntress-earth","name":"Yaoi Huntress Earth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1834_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"535"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-30T20:32:28-07:00","id":1110031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yaoi Huntress Earth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109548-dead-metis-storage-questions?p=1110028#post1110028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it wrong that I chuckled when I read the title of this thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hardly; it did start as a cheeky dark-humor &quot;Pulp Fiction&quot; shout-out after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-02T09:07:38-07:00","id":1110566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109548-dead-metis-storage-questions?p=1109979#post1109979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Those alcoholic Irish whoremongers</div> </div> </div> </div><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">This sentence is the essence of why we're giving you at least a month off from these forums.<br /> <br /> Everyone else may continue the dark humor aspect of this thread.</span></b><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/o...06-forum-rules</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>1. Respect other people</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don\u2019t personally attack other users, members of their gaming groups, and so on. Also, <b>don\u2019t attack groups of people</b>. That means avoiding racist, sexist, homophobic, transphobic and similar insults. Racial, sexual, and other slurs, as well as misgendering, count as insults. Please also avoid broad declarations that attack a group of people to get around making a \u201cpersonal\u201d attack. Like all rules, this rule applies equally to people working for Onyx Path, White Wolf, Paradox, and CCP.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b> Onyx Path Forum Moderator</b></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Read the rules</a><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">This is my mod voice.</span></b><br /> This is not my mod voice.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9-sparketh","name":"Sparketh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T12:35:38-07:00","id":1110948,"title":"","content":"(Hmm. I here I thought the rampant Celto<i>philia</i> of the old days was occasionally odd.)<br /> <br /> One of my favorite templates from the revised Tribebooks is still the Fianna Mule in Black. <br /> <br /> And, obviously, the best way to dispose of a metis corpse is with,<ul><li>A) A chain saw and a couple of gallons of lye</li> <li>B) A pig farm or</li> <li>C) Your local O'Tolley's</li> </ul><br /> More seriously, I think most tribes have a rite for that, similar to the Silent Strider method of summoning scarab spirits to devour a body so that the Eaters of the Dead can't desecrate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T14:34:27-07:00","id":1111014,"title":"","content":"There is also a rite...I can't remember which book but I have to hunt for it. It allows the Metis to pick what form it turns to when it dies. For the life of me I can't remember what book it was from and I don't have the time to pour over everything right now (though I'd hit up the revised CoG first...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T20:24:50-07:00","id":1111128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109548-dead-metis-storage-questions?p=1111014#post1111014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also a rite...I can't remember which book but I have to hunt for it. It allows the Metis to pick what form it turns to when it dies. For the life of me I can't remember what book it was from and I don't have the time to pour over everything right now (though I'd hit up the revised CoG first...)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the Guardians of the Caerns book if I'm not mistaken. I can't recall the name of the rite but it's the one I mentioned in my first post.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T20:40:22-07:00","id":1111131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109548-dead-metis-storage-questions?p=1111128#post1111128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the Guardians of the Caerns book if I'm not mistaken. I can't recall the name of the rite but it's the one I mentioned in my first post.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> *smacks forehead* Not sure how I missed that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-03T21:21:42-07:00","id":1111141,"title":"","content":"Nope, I was totally wrong actually. They talk about how to get rid of metis corpses but not the rite. I found it in the W20 core book. &quot;Last Blessing&quot; performed by the ritemaster to a dying or just deceased metis ensures the corpse takes the form of wolf or human, whichever the metis preferred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-24T10:26:45-07:00","id":1119938,"title":"","content":"It would be nice if there were a way to bring the dying metis or the dead body into the penumbra, but if you can't do that, and you don't have access to the rite, I'd suggest burning the body on a funeral pyre before transporting it, and then all you have to deal with is the bones. If you don't have enough time or private space to do that, wrap the body in some big, old blankets and quilts, get a van or an SUV and lots of smelly &quot;cargo&quot; like crates of flowers or scented candles to cover the smell of the dead body, because even if it's not bloody or rotting, a big crinos body will still probably have a strong odor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T11:29:43-07:00","id":1120921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109548-dead-metis-storage-questions?p=1109725#post1109725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1A.<br /> I think you'd have to dismember it but...maybe? The problem is the weight. You could fill a trunk with clothing but I wouldn't even try to fill one with books. At 900 lbs...that's a lot of weight. You generally need a trailer for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>900 pounds? There's no way that even Metis with the Huge Size merit would be <i>that</i> heavy. I'm no expert on this stuff but even really serious bodybuilders wouldn't get much heavier than 200 pounds. and since metis weigh approximately 150% their weight in homid form; the heaviest would average out around 450 lbs. (if I'm wrong about that, again I'm no expert) <i>with </i>the Huge Size merit I wouldn't imagine anymore than a 100 pound increase at the <i>absolute </i>most (again, my rushed math is probably way off but if anything I'm probably over estimating so it kinda works out)<br /> <br /> Even if you had a whole pack assigned to transport a metis corpse somewhere in a car, if they all took homid form the weight wouldn't be a real problem. Especially if they had a van or a pickup truck or something, an average five-seater would have more of a space problem since crinos are still 9 feet tall.<br /> <br /> Also I really like the idea of conditional Delerium for metis corpses; since they're obviously dead the fear response or however the Delerium works wouldn't trigger unless it already startled or took the human by surprise. For example; if a bunch of werewolves were fighting on top of a tall building and a metis gets decapitated and the head falls off the roof, anyone that the head landed near would freak out and run/pass out/etc.<br /> <br /> I'm using that in my chronicles now! Now all I have to do is hand them a dead metis...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13528-lordpyrus25","name":"LordPyrus25","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13528_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T12:58:38-07:00","id":1120977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordPyrus25</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109548-dead-metis-storage-questions?p=1120921#post1120921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 900 pounds? There's no way that even Metis with the Huge Size merit would be <i>that</i> heavy. I'm no expert on this stuff but even really serious bodybuilders wouldn't get much heavier than 200 pounds. and since metis weigh approximately 150% their weight in homid form; the heaviest would average out around 450 lbs. (if I'm wrong about that, again I'm no expert) <i>with </i>the Huge Size merit I wouldn't imagine anymore than a 100 pound increase at the <i>absolute </i>most (again, my rushed math is probably way off but if anything I'm probably over estimating so it kinda works out)</div> </div> </div> </div>Glabro form says it doubles (or triples) a Garou's Homid bodyweight.<br /> I seem to remember Crinos doubling that again. The W20 book list average Crinos body weight at 400-800lbs. So I agree 900 would certainly be abnormal, but it won't be outside of the realm of possibilities. A Crinos body should be transportable though, with some effort.<br /> <br /> I generally agree with the rest of the post. As per how to handle Delirium with a Metis corpse, I don't know. I've never really given it any thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T13:34:39-07:00","id":1120993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109548-dead-metis-storage-questions?p=1120977#post1120977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glabro form says it doubles (or triples) a Garou's Homid bodyweight.<br /> I seem to remember Crinos doubling that again. The W20 book list average Crinos body weight at 400-800lbs. So I agree 900 would certainly be abnormal, but it won't be outside of the realm of possibilities. A Crinos body should be transportable though, with some effort.<br /> <br /> I generally agree with the rest of the post. As per how to handle Delirium with a Metis corpse, I don't know. I've never really given it any thought.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah you're right about the weight increases, I just messed up the math (what else s new?) though I'll say that since most Garou start out as teen-aged or sometimes even younger they likely wouldn't go above 500 pounds in Crinos, so likely only adult metis would get that heavy.<br /> <br /> I was looking at one of my characters that I had calculated out the weight of (who incidentally, is a metis) and she went from 112 lbs. in Homid form to 392 in Crinos so I should have realized my mistake right away.<br /> <br /> It's weird that they never addressed how Delerium worked in regards to metis corpses considering a whole section of the Guardians of Caerns source book was about metis. They talked about body disposal (including the traditional Fianna method, which leads me to believe that whatever ancient Elder came up with it was a really messed up Garou) but not about what would happen if a human saw the corpse aside from the whole &quot;breach of the Veil&quot; thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13528-lordpyrus25","name":"LordPyrus25","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13528_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T15:03:39-07:00","id":1121563,"title":"","content":"I knew plenty of male athletes in high school who were between 150-250 pounds and more in college who were between 200-300 pounds. Since Garou tend to be athletic, I would expect them to range between 600-1200 pounds in Crinos (ranging between 150-300 pounds in Homid).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-27T16:48:11-07:00","id":1121619,"title":"","content":"You really can't estimate the crinos form's weight by scaling up a human form to 9 feet tall and adding muscle. With their huge arm span and general bulkiness, they seem to be built more like gorillas than humans. The thickness and density of their bones, muscles, and other organs is probably an apples to oranges comparison against humans or wolves, or really any natural species.<br /> <br /> I expect the Delirium would still have a serious effect on humans. It's a deeply rooted primal fear, so even if the encounter is with a dead body, horror, confusion, and denial would set in, though the human witness might not be as likely to flee for his life, or drop into a fetal position and hope the dead body doesn't attack him. If some ordinary human starts getting nosy, you might want to pass off the body as something like a grizzly bear or a large feral hog, since those can be pretty gigantic themselves. Anything a human sees that he shouldn't see could be converted in his memory by the Delirium into something like that, and the power of suggestion could help. Just don't let any high-willpowered biologists or conspiracy theorists get in your way, or you might have to add another dead body to your tally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T08:37:12-07:00","id":1123028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109548-dead-metis-storage-questions#post1109548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1A) Can the average dead metis fit inside the trunk of a car?<br /> 1B) And if so, would it be a viable method of disposal to drive said car to a &quot;car compacting facility&quot;, have the car cubed and melted like in &quot;Goldfinger&quot;, right?<br /> <br /> 2A) Would a dead metis corpse (being Crinos) still invoke The Delirium if spotted by a human who catches you dragging it across the road?<br /> 2B) If not, would it be an efficient idea to have said Metis be dried, stuffed, taxidermied and passed off as an exhibit in a wax-museum/theme-restaurant/circus/roller coaster ride? As a prop, it would be the perfect cover, wouldn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) I'd say no. Crinos are three meters high and 300 kg heavy, they're basically as big as half of the car and 1/3rd as heavy. The torso is also quite bulky, and that alone could be too big to close the trunk.<br /> <br /> 2A) I'd say no to that either. Unsettling, sure, but if I got it right the metis' bodies are a real danger for the Veil (if they triggered Delirium they wouldn't be so risky). After all, the Delirium is a supernatural/psychological effect and it kinda makes sense that requires a live, roaring garou to be triggered. Anything dead is way less scary. But it's just my opinion, you could rule that the shape alone is enough to cause Delirium, it would make sense too.<br /> <br /> 2B) You could, but I'd remove one point of <u>permanent </u>Honor renown to any garou attempting this (unless they're bsd, in that case it's fine), and a few points of wisdom too (yes, it looks like a prop but if some hunter, journalist or government agent finds it you just gave him the DNA proof that werewolves are real). Yes, they're metis and bastards and pariah, it's still an act against a warrior of Gaia that stinks of the Wyrm. Note: this does not mean that a group of Garous can't do it, just that the Garou and spirit society won't look at it with favour.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T20:22:26-07:00","id":1123291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1109548-dead-metis-storage-questions?p=1110948#post1110948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And, obviously, the best way to dispose of a metis corpse is with...<br /> Your local O'Tolley's...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ewwww... So<i> that's </i>how the Black Spirals get rid of all of theirs. I always wondered.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T03:08:25-07:00","id":1123817,"title":"","content":"Not to mention why people go so bonkers and crazy eating O-Tooley's: You are what you eat after all <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}